    "body": "First of all, congrats on getting this published! I watched a bit from the sidelines and it seemed like quite the undertaking. Glad things are quite a bit better now. (Probably too late for `text/json` :-).)\r\n\r\nMaybe we should reference the new RFC here:\r\n\r\n> Servers should use [text/javascript](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#text/javascript) for JavaScript resources. Servers should not use other [JavaScript MIME types](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#javascript-mime-type) for JavaScript resources, and must not use non-[JavaScript MIME types](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#javascript-mime-type).\r\n\r\nAt the end of the document we also have a list of MIME types, including a number of JavaScript MIME types. I think most of those can be removed as they are in fact no longer referenced in the document, except for `text/javascript`. And then after `text/javascript` there we can reference this RFC as well (perhaps replacing the Ecma-262 reference, not sure).",
